From a18addfc7f1855a5798b9a438ee94efd85947e0c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 09:48:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: remove an affiliated AP at the expiry of its timer

Depends on 186-ap-mld-announce-the-removal-of-an-affiliated-ap.patch,
which counts the AP Removal Timer and left the BSS running at 0.

The BSS kept beaconing until the caller reconfigured the AP MLD, 1.64 s
after the count reached 0 on MT7996 and 1.0 s on mac80211_hwsim.

hostapd sees no TBTT of the link: nl80211 reports neither a Beacon
transmission nor the TSF of an AP, and mt7996 gives the TSF of an
interface's default link only, through debugfs. The count now runs from
t1, the return of the first Beacon update with the count N, which is
the closest sign of the driver taking it. The first Beacon with N goes
out at a TBTT a in (t1, t1 + BI]; the update at t1 + k * BI comes
before the TBTT a + k * BI and gives that Beacon N - k. The expiry runs
at t1 + N * BI, after the Beacon with the count 1 and before a + N * BI,
the TBTT the count names. So no Beacon carries the reserved value 0 of
the AP Removal Timer, and no Beacon of the link goes out at or after
that TBTT. At the expiry, in this order:

- keep any Beacon update from rewriting the removed link;
- rewrite the Beacons of the other links, starting on a link that runs
  no channel or color switch, so that they drop the Reconfiguration
  element and the removed link's entry in the Reduced Neighbor Report
  before the wait below, and carry no count past the TBTT it names;
- free the link stations of the non-AP MLDs that keep another link
  (REMOVE_LINK_STA), so that the link STOP_AP flushes only the stations
  the link alone holds;
- send each station associated over the link a Disassociation where it
  is not an MLD, and a Deauthentication where it is: hostapd cannot
  move an association to another link, so it associates again. The
  Deauthentication goes out on a partner link, with the MLD address and
  that link's ID;
- wait for the TX status of these frames, for at most a quarter of a
  beacon interval, as the link STOP_AP drops the frames the driver still
  holds (mt7996 has no flush of a station's queues);
- stop the Beacon on that link (link STOP_AP);
- take the BSS out of the AP MLD, and rewrite the Beacons of the other
  links again, as the maximum number of simultaneous links in their
  Basic Multi-Link element counts each started link of the AP MLD
  (hostapd_get_active_links()), the removed link included until now.

Then call the ucode bss_link_removed hook, which removes the BSS the way
a configuration without it does. No group addressed Deauthentication
goes out on the removed link, as a non-AP MLD that still holds it would
end its whole association. The BSS delete reaches
hostapd_bss_link_deinit() a second time, which the guard of patch 182
makes a no-op for a BSS that already left the AP MLD.

For the ucode link_remove method, hostapd_link_remove_expiry_ms() gives
the time until the expiry, rounded down, and hostapd_link_remove_ms()
the time until the link stops at the latest, with the wait, rounded up.
Both count from the time the next count is due, so a repeated request
gets the time that is left. hostapd_mld_beacons_update() is exported
for a BSS that leaves the AP MLD another way.

A request for a link in a channel or color switch is refused: such a
link refuses a new Beacon, and the count would run without the
announcement. A request for a BSS in an MBSSID set with other BSSes is
refused as well: mac80211 stops the whole set when one of its links
stops.

IEEE 802.11be-2024 35.3.6.3 removes an affiliated AP from an AP MLD
that goes on. A request for a link is therefore refused where no other
link of the AP MLD beacons without a removal of its own. The expiry
checks again, as the other links can stop during the countdown. Such a
link then keeps running with its Beacon rewritten without the
Reconfiguration element, and the caller's configuration decides whether
it goes.

The limits of this timing:

- IEEE 802.11be-2024 35.3.6.3 has the BSS end at or after the TBTT the
  count names, and a Disassociation go out after that TBTT. Here both
  come up to one beacon interval before it, as hostapd cannot see the
  TBTT.
- The wait runs only where a station is associated over the link. Where
  it does, and the first TBTT came less than the wait after t1
  (a - t1 < BI / 4), the wait can span the TBTT the count names. The
  link then sends one more Beacon, the one with the count 1 again, while
  the other links already carry no Reconfiguration element. Without such
  a station, the link stops at the expiry, before that TBTT.
- Where the driver takes the first update only after a (a - t1 shorter
  than its update latency), every count lands one TBTT late, the named
  TBTT becomes a + (N + 1) * BI, and the link stops up to two beacon
  intervals before it. Counting from the return of the update keeps
  this to the latency of the driver behind that return.
- A frame to a station in power save stays buffered until the station
  wakes, and the station gets it only where it wakes within the wait.
- A channel or color switch that starts on a link during the countdown
  refuses that link's Beacon updates, and its Beacons keep the count
  they had until the switch ends.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
 src/ap/beacon.c     |    9 ++
 src/ap/hostapd.c    |  267 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 src/ap/hostapd.h    |    6 +
 src/ap/ieee802_11.c |    6 +
 src/ap/sta_info.h   |    1 
 5 files changed, 283 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

--- a/src/ap/beacon.c
+++ b/src/ap/beacon.c
@@ -2779,6 +2779,15 @@ static int __ieee802_11_set_beacon(struc
 		return -1;
 	}
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
+	if (hapd->eht_mld_link_removal_expired) {
+		wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG,
+			   "MLD: No Beacon for link_id=%u, it is being removed",
+			   hapd->mld_link_id);
+		return 0;
+	}
+#endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
+
 	if (hapd->csa_in_progress) {
 		wpa_printf(MSG_ERROR, "Cannot set beacons during CSA period");
 		return -1;
--- a/src/ap/hostapd.c
+++ b/src/ap/hostapd.c
@@ -492,6 +492,240 @@ static void hostapd_link_remove_timeout_
 }
 
 
+static unsigned int hostapd_link_remove_tx_wait_us(struct hostapd_data *hapd)
+{
+	return TU_TO_USEC(hapd->iconf->beacon_int) / 4;
+}
+
+
+static u64 hostapd_link_remove_expiry_us(struct hostapd_data *hapd)
+{
+	struct os_reltime now, left;
+	u64 us;
+
+	if (!hapd->eht_mld_link_removal_count)
+		return 0;
+
+	us = (u64) (hapd->eht_mld_link_removal_count - 1) *
+		TU_TO_USEC(hapd->iconf->beacon_int);
+
+	os_get_reltime(&now);
+	if (os_reltime_before(&now, &hapd->eht_mld_link_removal_due)) {
+		os_reltime_sub(&hapd->eht_mld_link_removal_due, &now, &left);
+		us += (u64) left.sec * 1000000 + left.usec;
+	}
+
+	return us;
+}
+
+
+/* Rounded down: the caller stops rendering the link no later than the
+ * expiry. */
+u64 hostapd_link_remove_expiry_ms(struct hostapd_data *hapd)
+{
+	return hostapd_link_remove_expiry_us(hapd) / 1000;
+}
+
+
+/* Rounded up, with the wait for the TX status of the frames at the expiry: the
+ * caller commits no earlier than the link stops. */
+u64 hostapd_link_remove_ms(struct hostapd_data *hapd)
+{
+	if (!hapd->eht_mld_link_removal_count)
+		return 0;
+
+	return (hostapd_link_remove_expiry_us(hapd) +
+		hostapd_link_remove_tx_wait_us(hapd) + 999) / 1000;
+}
+
+
+static bool hostapd_link_remove_pending(struct hostapd_data *hapd)
+{
+	return hapd->eht_mld_link_removal_count ||
+		hapd->eht_mld_link_removal_expired;
+}
+
+
+static struct hostapd_data *
+hostapd_link_remove_partner(struct hostapd_data *hapd, struct sta_info *sta)
+{
+	struct hostapd_data *link_bss;
+
+	for_each_mld_link(link_bss, hapd) {
+		if (link_bss == hapd || !link_bss->started ||
+		    !link_bss->beacon_set_done ||
+		    hostapd_link_remove_pending(link_bss))
+			continue;
+
+		if (sta && !sta->mld_info.links[link_bss->mld_link_id].valid)
+			continue;
+
+		return link_bss;
+	}
+
+	return NULL;
+}
+
+
+/* Start on a link without a channel or color switch, which refuses a new
+ * Beacon and would stop the rest. */
+void hostapd_mld_beacons_update(struct hostapd_data *hapd)
+{
+	struct hostapd_data *link_bss;
+
+	for_each_mld_link(link_bss, hapd) {
+		if (!link_bss->started || !link_bss->beacon_set_done ||
+		    link_bss->csa_in_progress)
+			continue;
+
+#ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211AX
+		if (link_bss->cca_in_progress)
+			continue;
+#endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211AX */
+
+		ieee802_11_set_beacon(link_bss);
+		return;
+	}
+}
+
+
+static void hostapd_link_remove_finish(void *eloop_data, void *user_ctx)
+{
+	struct hostapd_data *hapd = eloop_data;
+
+	eloop_cancel_timeout(hostapd_link_remove_finish, hapd, NULL);
+
+	hostapd_drv_stop_ap(hapd);
+
+	/* A group addressed Deauthentication would end the association of each
+	 * non-AP MLD (IEEE Std 802.11be-2024, 11.3.4.5) */
+	hapd->conf->broadcast_deauth = 0;
+
+	wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG, "MLD: Removal timer expired, link_id=%u stopped",
+		   hapd->mld_link_id);
+
+	hostapd_bss_link_deinit(hapd);
+	hostapd_mld_beacons_update(hapd);
+
+	hostapd_ucode_bss_cb(hapd, "bss_link_removed");
+}
+
+
+static bool hostapd_link_remove_sta_addr(struct sta_info *sta, const u8 *addr)
+{
+	unsigned int i;
+
+	if (ether_addr_equal(sta->addr, addr))
+		return true;
+
+	for (i = 0; i < MAX_NUM_MLD_LINKS; i++)
+		if (sta->mld_info.links[i].valid &&
+		    ether_addr_equal(sta->mld_info.links[i].peer_addr, addr))
+			return true;
+
+	return false;
+}
+
+
+/* The status can arrive on any link of the AP MLD */
+void hostapd_link_remove_tx_status(struct hostapd_data *hapd, const u8 *addr)
+{
+	struct hostapd_data *link_bss;
+	struct sta_info *sta;
+
+	if (!hapd->conf->mld_ap || !hapd->mld)
+		return;
+
+	for_each_mld_link(link_bss, hapd) {
+		if (!link_bss->eht_mld_link_removal_tx)
+			continue;
+
+		for (sta = link_bss->sta_list; sta; sta = sta->next) {
+			if (!sta->link_removal_tx ||
+			    !hostapd_link_remove_sta_addr(sta, addr))
+				continue;
+
+			sta->link_removal_tx = false;
+			if (--link_bss->eht_mld_link_removal_tx)
+				break;
+
+			eloop_cancel_timeout(hostapd_link_remove_finish,
+					     link_bss, NULL);
+			eloop_register_timeout(0, 0, hostapd_link_remove_finish,
+					       link_bss, NULL);
+			break;
+		}
+	}
+}
+
+
+/* A non-AP MLD gets a Deauthentication on a partner link, as hostapd
+ * cannot move an association to another link. */
+static void hostapd_link_remove_notify_stas(struct hostapd_data *hapd)
+{
+	struct hostapd_data *tx_hapd;
+	struct sta_info *sta;
+	int res;
+
+	for (sta = hapd->sta_list; sta; sta = sta->next) {
+		if (!(sta->flags & WLAN_STA_ASSOC))
+			continue;
+
+		if (ap_sta_is_mld(hapd, sta)) {
+			tx_hapd = hostapd_link_remove_partner(hapd, sta);
+			if (!tx_hapd)
+				tx_hapd = hapd;
+			res = hostapd_drv_sta_deauth(tx_hapd, sta->addr,
+						     WLAN_REASON_DEAUTH_LEAVING);
+		} else {
+			res = hostapd_drv_sta_disassoc(
+				hapd, sta->addr,
+				WLAN_REASON_DISASSOC_STA_HAS_LEFT);
+		}
+
+		if (res)
+			continue;
+
+		sta->link_removal_tx = true;
+		hapd->eht_mld_link_removal_tx++;
+	}
+}
+
+
+static void hostapd_link_remove_expire(struct hostapd_data *hapd)
+{
+	unsigned int wait_us;
+
+	if (!hostapd_link_remove_partner(hapd, NULL)) {
+		wpa_printf(MSG_INFO,
+			   "MLD: Keep link_id=%u, no other link beacons",
+			   hapd->mld_link_id);
+		ieee802_11_set_beacon(hapd);
+		return;
+	}
+
+	hapd->eht_mld_link_removal_expired = true;
+	hapd->beacon_set_done = 0;
+	hostapd_mld_beacons_update(hapd);
+	hostapd_free_link_stas(hapd);
+	hostapd_link_remove_notify_stas(hapd);
+
+	if (!hapd->eht_mld_link_removal_tx) {
+		hostapd_link_remove_finish(hapd, NULL);
+		return;
+	}
+
+	wait_us = hostapd_link_remove_tx_wait_us(hapd);
+	wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG,
+		   "MLD: Removal timer expired, link_id=%u waits up to %u us for %u frames",
+		   hapd->mld_link_id, wait_us, hapd->eht_mld_link_removal_tx);
+	eloop_register_timeout(0, wait_us, hostapd_link_remove_finish, hapd,
+			       NULL);
+}
+
+
+/* hostapd sees no TBTT: the countdown runs from the return of the first
+ * Beacon update and expires before the TBTT that the count names. */
 static void hostapd_link_remove_timeout_handler(void *eloop_data,
 						void *user_ctx)
 {
@@ -505,13 +739,12 @@ static void hostapd_link_remove_timeout_
 		   hapd->mld_link_id,
 		   hapd->eht_mld_link_removal_count);
 
-	ieee802_11_set_beacon(hapd);
-
 	if (!hapd->eht_mld_link_removal_count) {
-		hostapd_free_link_stas(hapd);
+		hostapd_link_remove_expire(hapd);
 		return;
 	}
 
+	ieee802_11_set_beacon(hapd);
 	hostapd_link_remove_timeout_register(hapd);
 }
 
@@ -524,9 +757,29 @@ int hostapd_link_remove(struct hostapd_d
 	    count > 0xffff)
 		return -1;
 
-	if (hapd->eht_mld_link_removal_count)
+	if (hostapd_link_remove_pending(hapd))
 		return 0;
 
+	if (hapd->csa_in_progress)
+		return -1;
+
+#ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211AX
+	if (hapd->cca_in_progress)
+		return -1;
+#endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211AX */
+
+	/* mac80211 stops each BSS of an MBSSID set together with the one
+	 * whose link stops at the expiry. */
+	if (hapd->iconf->mbssid && hapd->iface->num_bss > 1)
+		return -1;
+
+	if (!hostapd_link_remove_partner(hapd, NULL)) {
+		wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG,
+			   "MLD: Do not remove link_id=%u, the last link",
+			   hapd->mld_link_id);
+		return -1;
+	}
+
 	wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG,
 		   "MLD: Remove link_id=%u in %u beacons",
 		   hapd->mld_link_id, count);
@@ -537,10 +790,9 @@ int hostapd_link_remove(struct hostapd_d
 	if (hapd->eht_mld_bss_param_change == 255)
 		hapd->eht_mld_bss_param_change = 0;
 
+	ieee802_11_set_beacon(hapd);
 	os_get_reltime(&hapd->eht_mld_link_removal_due);
 	hostapd_link_remove_timeout_register(hapd);
-
-	ieee802_11_set_beacon(hapd);
 	return 0;
 }
 
@@ -551,7 +803,10 @@ void hostapd_free_hapd_data(struct hosta
 {
 #ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
 	eloop_cancel_timeout(hostapd_link_remove_timeout_handler, hapd, NULL);
+	eloop_cancel_timeout(hostapd_link_remove_finish, hapd, NULL);
 	hapd->eht_mld_link_removal_count = 0;
+	hapd->eht_mld_link_removal_expired = false;
+	hapd->eht_mld_link_removal_tx = 0;
 #endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
 
 	os_free(hapd->probereq_cb);
--- a/src/ap/hostapd.h
+++ b/src/ap/hostapd.h
@@ -546,6 +546,8 @@ struct hostapd_data {
 	u16 eht_mld_link_removal_start;
 	u16 eht_mld_link_removal_count;
 	struct os_reltime eht_mld_link_removal_due;
+	bool eht_mld_link_removal_expired;
+	unsigned int eht_mld_link_removal_tx;
 #endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_NAN_USD
@@ -987,6 +989,10 @@ struct hostapd_data * hostapd_mld_get_li
 					       u8 link_id);
 int hostapd_link_remove(struct hostapd_data *hapd, u32 count);
 bool hostapd_link_remove_critical_update(struct hostapd_data *hapd);
+u64 hostapd_link_remove_expiry_ms(struct hostapd_data *hapd);
+u64 hostapd_link_remove_ms(struct hostapd_data *hapd);
+void hostapd_mld_beacons_update(struct hostapd_data *hapd);
+void hostapd_link_remove_tx_status(struct hostapd_data *hapd, const u8 *addr);
 bool hostapd_is_ml_partner(struct hostapd_data *hapd1,
 			   struct hostapd_data *hapd2);
 u8 hostapd_get_mld_id(struct hostapd_data *hapd);
--- a/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
+++ b/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
@@ -9122,10 +9122,16 @@ void ieee802_11_mgmt_cb(struct hostapd_d
 	case WLAN_FC_STYPE_DEAUTH:
 		wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG, "mgmt::deauth cb");
 		handle_deauth_cb(hapd, mgmt, len, ok);
+#ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
+		hostapd_link_remove_tx_status(hapd, mgmt->da);
+#endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
 		break;
 	case WLAN_FC_STYPE_DISASSOC:
 		wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG, "mgmt::disassoc cb");
 		handle_disassoc_cb(hapd, mgmt, len, ok);
+#ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
+		hostapd_link_remove_tx_status(hapd, mgmt->da);
+#endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
 		break;
 	case WLAN_FC_STYPE_ACTION:
 		wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG, "mgmt::action cb ok=%d", ok);
--- a/src/ap/sta_info.h
+++ b/src/ap/sta_info.h
@@ -352,6 +352,7 @@ struct sta_info {
 	 * transaction 1 is the only peer link address available for the reply.
 	 */
 	u8 auth_link_addr[ETH_ALEN];
+	bool link_removal_tx;
 #endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
 
 	u16 max_idle_period; /* if nonzero, the granted BSS max idle period in
